    "text": "Step 1: Turn off the water supply to the toilet tank. Locate the shut-off valve under the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water.\n\n***\nStep 2: Remove the toilet from the floor. Use a toilet wrench to loosen the bolts or nuts that secure the toilet to the floor. Once loose, lift the toilet up and remove it.\n\n***\nStep 3: Clean the toilet tank and bowl. Use a damp cloth to wipe away any dirt or debris from the tank and bowl. This will make the installation easier and prevent any issues with the new toilet.\n\n***\nStep 4: Install the new toilet. Position the new toilet in the same spot as the old one. Secure it with the bolts or nuts, making sure it's level and properly aligned.\n\n***\nStep 5: Turn the water supply back on and test the toilet. Open the water supply valve and check for leaks. If there are no leaks, the installation is complete.\n\nLet me know how it works. I can give you next steps when you finish all steps above.",
