   "text": "<<How to Install a Toilet Seat>>\n\nStep 1: Gather the necessary tools and materials. You will need a screwdriver, pliers, and a level.\n\n***\nStep 2: Remove the old toilet seat. Unplug the electrical cord and loosen the mounting bolts with a screwdriver. Carefully lift the seat off the toilet.\n\n***\nStep 3: Prepare the toilet bowl. Clean the bowl and ensure it is dry. Apply a small amount of plumber's putty around the edge of the new seat.\n\n***\nStep 4: Install the new seat. Position the seat over the toilet bowl and press it into place. Use the mounting bolts to secure the seat to the bowl.\n\n***\nStep 5: Connect the water supply. Turn on the water supply and check for leaks. If you detect a leak, turn off the water and recheck the connection.\n\n***\nStep 6: Test the seat. Turn on the water and test the seat for proper function. Ensure the seat moves smoothly and the water flows correctly.",
